/* ==========================================================================
 * AE_UNIVERSITIES -- education provider directory dataset
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 90 higher education institutions holding an **active institutional licence
 * from the UAE Ministry of Education's Commission for Academic Accreditation
 * (CAA)** -- the licence that lets an institution sponsor a student residence
 * visa. Generated by _tooling/build_dataset_ae.py -- do not hand-edit.
 *
 * SOURCES
 *   CAA register of licensed higher education institutions -- 156 rows, 102
 *     with an active licence. Captured 2026-06-16.
 *     https://caa.ae/Pages/Institutes/All.aspx
 *   CAA register of accredited academic programmes -- 2128 programmes, 1718
 *     active, joined by the register's own institution id. Captured 2025-04-18.
 *     https://caa.ae/Pages/Programs/All.aspx
 *   KHDA "Dubai's Private Higher Education Institutions" open data, used for
 *     Dubai campus districts and, where the programme capture predates an
 *     institution's licence, its Census 2024-2025 subject areas.
 *     https://web.khda.gov.ae/en/Resources/KHDA-s-data-statistics
 *   QS World University Rankings 2027, published 18 June 2026 -- 12 UAE
 *     universities, all 12 of them on this register.
 *
 * Both CAA captures come from the Internet Archive because caa.ae currently
 * answers its own register pages with "ERROR: Please try again later"; the
 * capture dates are above and in the builder.
 *
 * WHY EVERY INSTITUTION HERE CAN ENROL YOU
 *
 * A UAE student residence visa is sponsored by the institution, and only a
 * licensed institution can sponsor one. The licence IS the permission -- the
 * same relationship CRICOS has in Australia and EMGS has in Malaysia -- so the
 * cards' hardcoded "Intl. Admits: Yes" is true at the source and not an
 * inference.
 *
 * WHAT IS EXCLUDED, AND WHY
 *   12 of the 102 active licences cover institutions an international student
 *   cannot apply to, and every card here asserts the opposite:
 *     8  armed-forces and police colleges (UAE nationals in service only)
 *     2  government-service academies that publish a nationals-only rule
 *     1  whose register entry reads "ADMISSION OF NEW STUDENTS IS CURRENTLY
 *        SUSPENDED"
 *     1  unverifiable -- no working website, no accredited programme and no
 *        published admissions route
 *   Nothing is excluded on a judgement about quality. The list is asserted in
 *   the builder, so a register update cannot change it silently.
 *
 * FIELDS
 *
 *   accredited  the institution's number of CAA-accredited programmes, a real
 *               published count off the regulator's own register, in the slot
 *               the UK page fills with an invented `offerRate`. It is NOT a
 *               selectivity figure and the UI labels it "CAA accredited".
 *               "n/a" where the institution holds a licence but has no row in
 *               the programme capture -- overwhelmingly the branch campuses
 *               licensed in Dubai during 2025-26, after that capture was taken.
 *
 *   programs    the institution's three largest subject areas. Real published
 *               categories, never a guess: CAA's own programme disciplines
 *               ordered by number of accredited programmes, or -- for a Dubai
 *               institution with no CAA programme rows yet -- KHDA's census
 *               specialisations ordered by enrolment.
 *
 *   rank        position in this list. `ranked: true` means the position is a
 *               real QS World University Rankings 2027 place; QS covers
 *               exactly 12 UAE universities and they are the first 12 entries,
 *               which is exactly the number of "Rank #N" cards the home-page
 *               carousel renders. Everything after them is ordered
 *               alphabetically and carries `ranked: false`.
 *
 *   location    "District, Emirate" for Dubai (KHDA publishes the free-zone
 *               district), "City, Emirate" where the campus city differs from
 *               the emirate, and the bare emirate otherwise.
 *
 *   type        EDITORIAL. The register publishes no institution category, so
 *               this is the one field here that is ours. It describes how the
 *               institution is constituted, not its quality:
 *               "Federal Institution" is the Ministry of Education's three
 *               federal institutions, "International Branch Campus" a foreign
 *               university's own UAE campus, "Government Institution" one
 *               established by the federal or an emirate government, and
 *               "Private Institution" the rest.
 * ========================================================================== */

